; Under --dc the debit and credit columns are summed per posting.  An
; inferred amount keeps its recovered cost precision (BIGINT_COST_PREC,
; issue #1692) when it is the only posting in a column, even though the
; account holds other postings in the same commodity: Assets:B credits
; the inferred 0.4 Y, which its net total of 1 Y does not show.  The
; semantic bisimulation's gross comparison (test/semantic/check_all.py
; --gross) replays this journal through the oracle's opt-in --gross
; flag and C++'s --amount column reports, where the lone-inferred
; display rule must reproduce the 0.4 Y credit line.

2018-01-01 * Foo
    Assets:A                    2 X @ 0.2 Y
    Assets:B

2018-01-02 * Bar
    Assets:B                    1 Y
    Equity

test bal --dc --flat --no-total
           2 X              0            2 X  Assets:A
           1 Y          0.4 Y            1 Y  Assets:B
             0            1 Y           -1 Y  Equity
end test